1d4341a629b13306aeb795491b4458daff5de6d3
fix(hooks): task content must survive PostCommit's read-only skip

tryAgentCommitFastPath mints a trailer for an idle session on a fresh task
record alone — its empty-session guard exempts HasTaskContent — but PostCommit
then dropped that same session through the read-only skip, which fires when a
session has no tracked files. That is the defining shape of a read-only
subagent's record, so whenever another session claimed the committed files the
trailer was left dangling over a checkpoint nothing ever filled.

The skip predates task records and still read "no files" as "nothing to save";
records are themselves the evidence, and the materializer fills the checkpoint.
Reported by Cursor Bugbot against the pre-reshape spelling of the trigger.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
